  << /ActualText (    2\05613\056 Netbounce Placement agrees to provide its services for a period of six \0506\051 \n             months\054 commencing from the first day of marketing activity\056 If the candidate\n             does not secure a job placement within this six\055month period by declared \n             services\054 Netbounce Placement reserves the right to conclude and terminate the \n             services rendered under this agreement without further obligation\056\n\n    2\05614\056 This section outlines key policies related to the service period\054 including \n             handling independent job offers\054 the process and discretion involved in \n             securing sponsorships\054 and the consequences of non\055compliance with payment \n             obligations\056\n\n    2\05615\056 If the candidate is within the service period and receives an offer \n             independently\054 Netbounce will not be liable for any refund after one month as \n             clearly described in refund policy\056 Parallel marketing efforts may disrupt \n             marketing flow for the same profile and carry the risk of blacklisting\056\n\n    2\05616\056 Netbounce does not commit to providing jobs that offer sponsorship\056 Sponsorship \n             decisions are solely at the discretion of the employer based on their assessment of\n             the candidate\047s value\054 skills\054 and knowledge\056 If the Employers deem the candidate an \n             asset\054 they may choose to provide sponsorship\056 Based on past data\054 80\045 of  \n             candidates placed by Netbounce have  received sponsorship from employers\056\n\015\n    2\05617\056 If the candidate attempts to evade their obligations to Netbounce by  skipping \n             installments\054 making false promises\054 or engaging in any payment  delays\054 Netbounce \n             reserves the right to seek legal action\056 Such actions may  result in the cancellation of\n             the candidate\047s visa by USCIS or by their  respective university\047s DSO\054 as well as \n             potential termination from their  employer\056\n\n    2\05618\056 Netbounce will continue to provide services for a period of 6 months\054 after which \n             the service term will conclude\056\n\n3\056    NETBOUNCE\031S LIABILITIES\072\015\n\n3\0561\056 The Netbounce undertakes and agrees with the Candidate\072\015\n\n      a\051 To assist Candidate\054 in landing them a job that suits best to their profile\056\n\n      b\051 Netbounce is liable to provide the interviews of company that ensures a candidate \n          a 40 hours of work per week\056\050\n      c\051 Make available additional bonus Content to Candidates such as Templets\054 guides\054 \n          and study plans\056\n\n      d\051 Make available to the Candidate a support desk\054 to resolve any technical issues\054 \n          and to answer the questions specific to the training materials\056 \n     \n      e\051 Netbounce is liable for assisting the candidate with the background check process \n          and the onboarding process at the company where they are hired\056\n\n      f\051  Netbounce is liable to assist the candidate with background verification screening\056\015\n          If Netbounce fails to do so\054 the payment made by the candidate at the time of\015\n          receiving the offer letter will be refunded\054 and remarketing efforts will be\015initiated\056\015\n          )
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 3096 0 R
     /Pg 1240 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

